# Sports Screener — AI Predictor Fixes, Table Tennis Rebrand, League Expansion & New Sports

## Overview

This plan addresses four distinct, high-priority tasks discovered across the codebase:

1. **Rename "Rally" → "Table Tennis"** across all UI labels, SEO copy, and documentation (internal sport ID `rally` is preserved to avoid a database migration)
2. **Fix the AI Predictor Table Tennis tab** — the `rally` data pipeline currently maps to Motorsport/Formula/WRC sources in every API layer, causing football/soccer fixtures to appear in the Table Tennis predictor tab; fix it to fetch real Table Tennis data
3. **Expand league and tournament coverage** for all 6 existing sports — Football, Basketball, Ice Hockey, Table Tennis, Tennis, and Baseball
4. **Add new sports** — American Football, Rugby Union, Cricket, MMA/UFC, and Volleyball — with full Screener pages, Predictor tabs, API configurations, and data pipeline wiring

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The internal `rally` sport ID is preserved in the Convex schema and all backend types. Changing it would require a database migration that clears existing cached predictor matches. This plan keeps `rally` as the stable ID and only changes display labels. Confirm this is acceptable.

> [!WARNING]
> Adding 5 new sports (American Football, Rugby, Cricket, MMA, Volleyball) requires new Convex schema `v.literal()` entries which trigger a schema push. The Convex schema change is backward-compatible (additive only), but requires running `npx convex deploy` after execution.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> New sports available via The Odds API (`american_football_nfl`, `rugbyleague_nrl`, `cricket_*`, `mma_*`, `volleyball_*`) and OddsPapi (sport IDs 14, 16, 17, 43) need to be confirmed as active in the live API key environment. The plan implements graceful fallback if keys lack credits for specific leagues.

